{"name":"Beluga","hex":"#eff2f1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Beluga","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of beluga."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Beluga"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beluga (sturgeon)","blocks":[{"text":"The beluga, also known as the beluga sturgeon or great sturgeon, is a species of sturgeon, which are anadromous fish of the family Acipenseridae of the order Acipenseriformes. It is found primarily in the Caspian and Black Sea basins, and formerly in the Adriatic Sea. Based on maximum size, it is the third-most-massive living species of bony fish. Heavily fished for the female's valuable roe, known as beluga caviar, wild populations have been greatly reduced by overfishing and poaching, leading IUCN to classify the species as critically endangered."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/%D0%91%D1%96%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B3%D0%B0_%28Huso_huso%29.jpg/330px-%D0%91%D1%96%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B3%D0%B0_%28Huso_huso%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beluga_(sturgeon)"},{"title":"Beluga whale","blocks":[{"text":"The beluga whale or the white whale is an Arctic and sub-Arctic cetacean. It is one of two living members of the family Monodontidae, along with the narwhal, and the only member of the genus Delphinapterus. It is also known as the sea canary, due to its high-pitched calls; and the melonhead, though that more commonly refers to the melon-headed whale, which is an oceanic dolphin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Oceanogr%C3%A0fic_29102004.jpg/330px-Oceanogr%C3%A0fic_29102004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beluga_whale"},{"title":"Beluga (vodka)","blocks":[{"text":"Beluga Noble Vodka is a brand of Super-Premium vodka produced and bottled by Noblewood Group in Montenegro."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Beluga_Vodka_logo.png/330px-Beluga_Vodka_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beluga_(vodka)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Huso_huso_adult_juvenile.jpg/500px-Huso_huso_adult_juvenile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Huso_huso_adult_juvenile.jpg/500px-Huso_huso_adult_juvenile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Comparison between an adult (above) and a juvenile (below) Huso huso","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHuso_huso_adult_juvenile.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Beluga.JPG/500px-Beluga.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Beluga.JPG/1280px-Beluga.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Beluga.JPG/500px-Beluga.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 1000-kg, 4.17-m-long beluga fish from the Volga River (National Museum of Tatarstan, Kazan, Russia)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeluga.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Hausen_%28Huso_huso_L.%29editDOB.JPG/500px-Hausen_%28Huso_huso_L.%29editDOB.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Hausen_%28Huso_huso_L.%29editDOB.JPG/1280px-Hausen_%28Huso_huso_L.%29editDOB.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Hausen_%28Huso_huso_L.%29edit